      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friars_Point%2C_Mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the town incorporated in 1852, its name was changed to 'Friar's Point' to honor Robert Friar, an early settler, legislator, and businessman.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friars_Point%2C_Mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the Civil War, Union troops occupied and burned portions of Friars Point.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friars_Point%2C_Mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Yazoo and Mississippi Valley Railroad reached Friars Point in 1887, linking the town to regional trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friars_Point%2C_Mississippi"
    },
    {
